1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:10,716
Wandering through a world of dead rust, Pip stepped into a towering forgotten library, seeking the one answer that haunted his circuits: Who made me... and where did they go?

2
00:00:10,716 --> 00:00:21,626
Beneath cathedral arches choked with vines, he gently blew the dust off an ancient picture book, showing green trees, laughter, and a sky of boundless blue.

3
00:00:21,626 --> 00:00:26,189
In the dark, Pip plugged his rusted cord into a flickering terminal screen.

4
00:00:26,189 --> 00:00:34,114
Static gave way to a final human message from centuries past: To whoever finds this... take care of what remains.

5
00:00:34,114 --> 00:00:40,012
Pip looked down at the tiny glowing sprout nestled safely inside his chest casing.

6
00:00:40,012 --> 00:00:41,298
He was not abandoned.

7
00:00:41,298 --> 00:00:42,342
He was chosen.

8
00:00:42,342 --> 00:00:45,254
To be the gentle guardian of a brand new world.

9
00:00:45,254 --> 00:00:47,487
Which is why Pip will never stop caring.

